al  and I did everything that you know you  read a bit online and all the moms tell  you to do so cabbage in your bra and  like crazy massages and I was having hot  showers every hour and like dipping my  boobs into like a hot bath on all fours  it was like it was not bad so this past  weekend I just like kind of felt like  enough was enough I was dealing with the  worst case of block ducts I've had so  since like I gave birth it literally  felt like I had a million little knot in  both breasts I wasn't getting any milk  out I was totally miserable it was so  painful and I kind of felt like I should  I give up like is this the men's of my  breast feeding and pumping journey like  do I just throw in the towel right now I  was like sitting in the bath on Friday  night just crying like I couldn't even  like get myself out of the bath to like  just feed my son and move on and I  wanted to have a nice night with my  husband but I just felt so down on  myself like I really really let myself  down on that  so the next morning I had a lactation  consultant come over to my house to try  to relieve me of these blockages and  even she couldn't get them out but what  she did do was recommend that I go up  inside in the flange the the piece that  goes on my breast pump and that actually  made a world of a difference instantly  as soon as I tried it Thank You Amazon  Prime for sending it so quickly but as  soon as I tried it I started to feel the  blockages coming out and I was starting  to get more milk out in each and every  pump so pumping Mama's if you are  constantly getting block duct or  mastitis maybe consider getting your  flange size re-evaluated I had no idea  that this was gonna make that kind of  difference also what I did yesterday was  I went to see an acupuncturist who  specializes in kind of milk ducts and  mastitis and not only does he do some  acupuncture but she also did some like  manual manipulation which was brutally  painful imagine having your nipple like